<section class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>Why Zena?</h2>
    <p>Engineered for WebAssembly GC, bringing the best of modern mainstream language design to the web and beyond.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="features-grid">
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon wasm">🎯</div>
      <h3>Wasm GC Native</h3>
      <p>Zena compiles exclusively to Wasm GC and is carefully designed from the start to produce small and fast Wasm binaries.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>No allocator or garbage collector is shipped with Zena modules</li>
        <li>Primitives, references, and arrays all map directly to Wasm GC types</li>
        <li>Type system prevents types that would require boxing or tagging in Wasm</li>
        <li>Strings are unicode safe and compile to fast host-specific encodings</li>
        <li>Polymorphic functions, dynamic dispatch, and inline classes are implemented with minimal runtime overhead</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon perf">⚡</div>
      <h3>Tiny & Fast Binaries</h3>
      <p>Wasm-optimized language design and an advanced optimizing compiler produce minimal, ultra-fast binaries.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>No runtime other than Wasm GC and a few string helpers</li>
        <li>Aggressive dead-code elimination removes unused code and types</li>
        <li>Devirtualization resolves virtual method calls to direct calls when possible</li>
        <li>Monomorphized generics produce optimal code for each concrete type</li>
        <li>(Future) Compiler flags control monomorphization, allowing developers to tune output for binary size vs. runtime speed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon familiar">📝</div>
      <h3>Familiar, Predictable &amp; Refined</h3>
      <p>Zena combines a TypeScript-like syntax with the best language features from Swift, Dart, Scala, Go, and Kotlin.</p>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Real primitive numeric types</li>
        <li>No implicit numeric coercions or surprising behaviors</li>
        <li>Clear separation between nominal types (classes, interfaces) and structural types (records and tuples)</li>
        <li>Lexical scoping and lexical `this` references</li>
        <li>Immutability by default</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon types">🔷</div>
      <h3>Prioritizing Correctness</h3>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Sound type system with no escape hatches</li>
        <li>Non-nullable references by default</li>
        <li>Guaranteed class initialization via initializer lists</li>
        <li>Exhaustive match checking</li>
        <li>No implicit coercions or truthy/falsy surprises</li>
        <li>Runtime-checked type casts</li>
        <li>(Future) Pre/post contracts &amp; unit types</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon modern">✨</div>
      <h3>Modern Ergonomics</h3>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Expression-oriented blocks (if, try, throw)</li>
        <li>Pattern matching with exhaustiveness checking</li>
        <li>Algebraic Data Types (sealed classes &amp; unions)</li>
        <li>Multi-valued function returns</li>
        <li>Pipelines (<code>|&gt;</code>) for clean chaining</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon toolchain">🛠️</div>
      <h3>Integrated Toolchain</h3>
      <p>A single CLI encompassing the compiler, test runner, LSP, formatter, and future linting/MCP tools. All tools are written in Zena itself and run natively on Wasm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon wasi">🧩</div>
      <h3>WASI &amp; WIT Integration</h3>
      <p>Import and export WASI components directly with no additional "bindgen" wrappers or external tools. Zena understands WIT files natively (in progress).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon stdlib">🔋</div>
      <h3>Rich Standard Library</h3>
      <p>Building on top of WASI plus Zena-specific modules, aiming for a "batteries included" stdlib with testing, CLI utilities, file systems, HTTP networking, and regex (in progress).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon future">🚀</div>
      <h3>Future Evolution</h3>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>Async/await cooperative concurrency</li>
        <li>Compile-time physical unit types</li>
        <li>Pre- and post-condition contracts</li>
        <li>Macros and code generation</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

